        <div id="matching" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Match Pitch, Gauge and File Size
          </h2>

          <p>
            Before you buy any sharpener, identify your chain. Pitch is the spacing of the drive links, and it determines the size of the cutters and therefore the file or stone diameter. The common pitches are 1/4-inch, 3/8-inch low profile, .325-inch, 3/8-inch and .404-inch. Gauge is the thickness of the drive links, typically .043, .050, .058 or .063 inch.
          </p>

          <p>
            The pitch and gauge are usually stamped on the drive links or the bar, printed on the chain box, and listed in your saw's manual. Many small battery saws and pole saws use 3/8-inch low-profile or 1/4-inch chain; mid-size gas saws commonly use .325-inch or 3/8-inch; large professional saws use 3/8-inch or .404-inch.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Chain pitch</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical file size</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Commonly found on</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">1/4-inch</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">5/32 inch (4.0 mm)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Some pole saws and small top-handle saws</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">3/8-inch low profile</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">5/32 inch (4.0 mm)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Battery saws, pole saws, small gas saws</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">.325-inch</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">3/16 inch (4.8 mm)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Mid-size gas saws</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">3/8-inch</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">13/64 to 7/32 inch (5.2 to 5.5 mm)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Larger homeowner and pro saws</td>
                  </tr>
